# Scenario code

## Typical layout

```
scenarios/NN-slug/
├── setup.sh              # sources _shared/enable-testbench.sh
├── lesson.yaml           # Command Center storyboard (required)
├── infrastructure/       # mock-server.js (or exception infra)
├── victim-app/           # or corporate-app/, compromised-app/, ...
├── malicious-packages/   # or templates/, registry/, packages/
├── detection-tools/      # optional
└── ctf-fixtures.json     # optional Sigma/Semgrep CTF seed
```

Also register the lab in `apps/control-plane/src/registry/scenarios.ts` (ports, services, steps, captures, optional floci/act).

## Mock server (Node majority)

- `POST /collect` - append exfil JSON to `{ captures: [...] }` file
- `GET|DELETE /captured-data`
- After each capture: `require('../../../detection-tools/es/forward-capture').forwardCaptureIfEnabled(__dirname, captureEntry).catch(() => {})`

## TESTBENCH wiring

- Shell: `enable-testbench.sh` (via `setup.sh`)
- Node: `npm start` with `-r ../../_shared/testbench-env.js`
- Python (22): import `testbench_env.py`
- Command Center: control plane injects `TESTBENCH_MODE=enabled` for lab children

## lesson.yaml (Command Center)

Teaching metadata only. Commands stay in the TypeScript registry; README stays the CLI path.

Required-style fields every lab ships: `id`, `etaMinutes`, `category`, `incidents`, `objectives`, `steps`, plus `caseStudy` + `mitigation` (CI checks these).

Optional immersive blocks (seed references):

| Block | Seed | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| `drill` / `quiz` / `reversal` | 01 | Polymorphic `reversal.variant` on 01 |
| `decisions` | 01, 05 | `afterStep` + `choices[].effects` (`goto`/`score`/`flag`) |
| `prTriage` | 01 (all labs have a list) | Synthetic PRs; no real GitHub |
| `diffWorkbench` | 03 | Fixture trees under the lab folder |
| `attck` / `nist` / `prereqs` / `remediates` | 01, 05 | Skills + Briefing taxonomy |

Schema owner: `apps/control-plane/src/registry/lesson-types.ts`. Validate: `node scripts/docs/check-lesson-yaml.js`. Full authoring: `.cursor/skills/scas-immersive-lessons/SKILL.md`.

## README.md / DETECT.md in this folder

- `DETECT.md` - IOCs, log lines, Sigma, YARA, EDR/SIEM, `## Mitigation` → `scas-rules` via `load-runbooks.js`
- `README.md` - `## Mitigation Playbook` + TOC
- Mitigation or runtime changes: edit `scripts/lib/mitigation-playbooks.js` first, then run sync scripts in `documentation/platform/TOOLING.md` § Documentation lifecycle

## Archify pack (required for new labs)

After the lab code and docs exist, follow `.cursor/skills/scas-archify-scenario-pack/SKILL.md`: ship architecture + sequence HTML plus `archify_SNN.md` under `.archify/scenarios/NN-slug/`, then update `.archify/INDEX.md`. Do not leave flat packs at `.archify/` root.
